# THE LIVE LEGS RUN INSIDE LINUX CONTAINERS, FROM THE WORKING TREE. With core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout hands bash a CRLF script, which fails at line 1 with `set: pipefail: invalid
# option name` and then a syntax error hundreds of lines later — a failure that looks like the leg
# and is the checkout. Pin the endings so a fresh clone runs what this one runs.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
